      "target": "claude",
      "type": "instructions",
    },
    {
      "code": "suspicious-value",
      "message": "postToolUse matcher "Write|Edit" uses Claude tool names, which never match in Cursor (Edit → Write). Give the matcher per-target values, e.g. matcher: { claude: "Edit", cursor: "Write" }",
      "path": undefined,
      "severity": "warn",
      "source": undefined,
      "target": "cursor",
      "type": "hooks",
    },
    {
      "code": "served-by",
      "message": "claude reads the AGENTS.md files too, so uac skips claude's own instructions output. Usually you only need one of these targets on a machine: set \`targets\` in universal-ai-config.overrides.ts (\`uac setup\` writes it). claude loses: file-pattern scoping (\`paths\` globs); nested AGENTS.md files load only when Claude reads a file in that folder, and none load while a non-empty CLAUDE.md, .claude/CLAUDE.md or CLAUDE.local.md exists",
      "path": undefined,
      "severity": "warn",
      "source": undefined,
      "target": "claude",
      "type": "instructions",
    },
    {
      "code": "served-by",
      "message": "copilot reads the AGENTS.md files too, so uac skips copilot's own instructions output. Usually you only need one of these targets on a machine: set \`targets\` in universal-ai-config.overrides.ts (\`uac setup\` writes it). copilot loses: \`applyTo\` patterns, \`excludeAgent\` and \`name\`; nested AGENTS.md files load only after Copilot views a file in that folder (CLI 1.0 and later)",
      "path": undefined,
      "severity": "warn",
      "source": undefined,
      "target": "copilot",
      "type": "instructions",
    },
    {
      "code": "served-by",
      "message": "copilot reads claude's hooks too, so uac skips copilot's own hooks output. Usually you only need one of these targets on a machine: set \`targets\` in universal-ai-config.overrides.ts (\`uac setup\` writes it). copilot loses: Copilot-only events (userPromptTransformed, preMcpToolCall, postResult, prePRDescription), \`cwd\`/\`env\`, and hooks in the GitHub cloud agent, which reads only .github/hooks. Copilot runs Claude-format hooks with Claude's tool names and payloads, and exit code 1 blocks the tool",
      "path": undefined,
      "severity": "warn",
      "source": undefined,
      "target": "copilot",
      "type": "hooks",
    },
    {
      "code": "served-by",
